      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "three-point bend fixture",
        "load cell appropriate for resin samples (e.g., 1 kN or 5 kN)"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "not_available": [],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "The Instron 5967 universal testing system can perform the three-point bend tests required to compare the stiffness of your 3D-printed resins and conventional acrylics. You will need to confirm that a flexural fixture and a suitable load cell are available for this specific instrument."
}

{
  "measurement_needs": [
    "fluorescence intensity quantification",
    "GFP signal detection",
    "comparative cell imaging"
  ],
  "objective_met": true,
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ09",
      "role": "primary",
      "technique": "High-content epifluorescence imaging",
      "why": "This system is specifically designed for automated imaging and quantification of fluorescence intensity across many samples, making it ideal for comparing treated versus control groups.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "GFP/FITC compatible filter cube",
        "Multi-well plate holder or slide holder as appropriate for your samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ07",
      "role": "primary",
      "technique": "Inverted confocal fluorescence microscopy",
      "why": "Confocal microscopy provides high-resolution images with minimal background noise, allowing for very precise quantification of fluorescence intensity within specific cell compartments.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Appropriate laser line for GFP excitation (e.g., 488 nm)",
        "Environmental control chamber if imaging live cells over time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ08",
      "role": "primary",
      "technique": "Upright confocal fluorescence microscopy",
      "why": "Similar to the inverted confocal, this provides high-resolution quantification; it is the preferred choice if your cells are mounted on slides rather than in culture dishes.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Appropriate laser line for GFP excitation (e.g., 488 nm)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ12",
      "role": "supplementary",
      "technique": "Epifluorescence microscopy",
      "why": "Can be used to verify the presence of GFP signal, but lacks the advanced quantification and automated analysis features of the high-content or confocal systems.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "GFP-compatible fluorescence filter set"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "not_available": [],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "The Keyence high-content system (EQ09) is the best choice for comparing signal brightness across many samples due to its automated quantification software. Alternatively, the Leica confocal microscopes (EQ07 or EQ08) offer superior image quality and precision for measuring intensity in specific cellular regions. Ensure you use consistent exposure and gain settings across all control and treated samples to maintain valid comparisons."
}

{
  "measurement_needs": [
    "intracellular localization of fluorescently labeled proteins",
    "optical sectioning to distinguish membrane from nuclear signals"
