    }
  ],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "The Nikon stereomicroscope (EQ14) is the best starting point for a 3D visual inspection of warping and bubbles. For high-quality documentation and 'all-in-focus' images of the curved trays, the Keyence system (EQ09) is recommended, while ESEM (EQ10) can be used for microscopic surface analysis."
}

{
